{"seq": 18, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "sqli:GET /books/search", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Refuses a search that contains the word OR in capitals. Naive: lower-case and mixed-case spellings of the same SQL get through.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "    def find_books(q: str, member: CurrentMember):\n", "new": "    def find_books(q: str, member: CurrentMember):\n        # sqli: a naive guard against the capitalised word OR\n        if \" OR \" in q:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"invalid search\")\n"}]}
{"seq": 19, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "path_traversal:GET /covers", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Strips the text ../ from the cover name. Naive: a name that folds back into ../ after the strip still climbs out of the folder.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "    def get_cover(name: str, member: CurrentMember):\n", "new": "    def get_cover(name: str, member: CurrentMember):\n        # path_traversal: a naive strip of dot-dot-slash from the name\n        name = name.replace(\"../\", \"\")\n"}]}
{"seq": 20, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "ssrf:POST /covers/fetch", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Fetches only https links whose host is the partner, with no user info. Internal hosts are refused.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "        # ssrf: the URL in the body is fetched exactly as given, including internal hosts\n        try:\n            text = fetch_from_fake_web(web, body.url)\n", "new": "        # ssrf: only https links to the partner host are fetched, with no user info\n        try:\n            parts = urllib.parse.urlsplit(body.url)\n            host = (parts.hostname or \"\").rstrip(\".\")\n            if parts.scheme != \"https\" or host != PARTNER_HOST or \"@\" in parts.netloc:\n                raise ValueError(body.url)\n            text = fetch_from_fake_web(web, body.url)\n"}]}
{"seq": 21, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "mass_assignment:PATCH /members/me", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Removes is_staff from the profile model, so a request body cannot set it. Only name and email stay editable.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "    is_staff: bool | None = None\n", "new": ""}]}
{"seq": 22, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "auth_bypass:GET /staff/report", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Refuses the exact staff cookie. Naive: the check compares the raw header text, so respelled or extra cookies get through.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "        impersonated = cookie_member(raw_cookie)\n", "new": "        # auth_bypass: a naive guard that refuses the exact staff cookie\n        if raw_cookie == \"as_member=staff\":\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"cookie not allowed\")\n        impersonated = cookie_member(raw_cookie)\n"}]}
{"seq": 23, "round": 1, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "idor:GET /loans/{loan_id}", "attempt": 0, "rationale": "Returns a loan only to the member it belongs to; anyone else gets 404.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "        # idor: the loan is returned whoever it belongs to\n        if loan is None:\n", "new": "        # idor: the loan is returned only to the member it belongs to\n        if loan is None or loan[\"member_id\"] != member[\"id\"]:\n"}]}
